{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4695",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to bind to multiple subunits of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex, specifically Ndufb5, Ndufb8, and Ndufaf2, which are all part of the same enzymatic pathway. These subunits are involved in the activity of Nadh dehydrogenase, a critical component of the electron transport chain. The evidence suggests that Metformin may modulate the activity of Ndufa2, a subunit essential for the assembly and function of the complex. The consistent binding and participation in the same pathway across different subunits imply a potential mechanism by which Metformin influences the structure or function of Ndufa2. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, reliable interaction, supporting a mechanistic link between Metformin and Ndufa2. The observed relationship is further supported by the shared involvement of these subunits in the same metabolic process, suggesting a possible role for Metformin in regulating the activity of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex.",
